{
 "method": {
  "name": "conformal risk control of the false-negative rate (as published; not new)",
  "reference": "Angelopoulos, A. N., Bates, S., Fisch, A., Lei, L., Schuster, T. Conformal Risk Control. ICLR 2024. arXiv:2208.02814",
  "statement": "For exchangeable losses L_i(lambda), non-increasing and right-continuous in lambda, bounded by B, with L_i(lambda_max) <= alpha: lambda_hat = inf{lambda : n/(n+1) R_n(lambda) + B/(n+1) <= alpha} (lambda_max if empty) gives E[L_{n+1}(lambda_hat)] <= alpha (Theorem 1). Here lambda = -t for a score threshold t, lambda_max = the floor t_min, B = 1.",
  "unit": "scene (frames of one video are not exchangeable)",
  "evaluation": "leave one scene out: t_hat from the other N - 1 scenes, held-out FNR at it"
 },
 "definitions": {
  "loss": "a scene's FNR at t: share of its population object-views that no box with score >= t covers (2D IoU >= 0.3 with the object's visible 2D box; any box, no one-to-one)",
  "population": "present: the pipeline's presence (visible 2D box, visible fraction above the presence threshold, from the reference depth); clearly_visible: the question generator's referent thresholds",
  "fnr_one_to_one": "FNR under the Hungarian 2D pairing of match_detections_2d against every present object (the pipeline's recall); reported, not controlled",
  "floor_fnr": "a scene's FNR at the CRC floor t_min (the lowest threshold CRC may choose); Theorem 1 assumes it is <= alpha",
  "box_cap": "a view with max_boxes boxes is truncated at thresholds up to its lowest written score (its cap floor); t_cap is the largest cap floor. Above t_cap the losses are the uncapped labeller's; at or below it they are exact for the capped labeller as run and an upper bound for an uncapped one. truncation=floor: CRC chooses only above t_cap; mark: anywhere, with in_truncated_region and share_views_truncated reported",
  "feasible": "some threshold met the CRC condition; if not, t_hat = t_min and no guarantee is claimed",
  "unmatched_to_annotation": "kept boxes with 2D IoU below the threshold against every present annotated object; ARKitScenes annotates 17 furniture classes, so these are not necessarily false",
  "range": "distance from the camera centre to the ground-truth box centre (m)",
  "mean_heldout_fnr": "mean over scenes of the held-out FNR at the threshold calibrated on the other scenes. It is at most alpha by construction whenever the mean floor FNR over all scenes is (loso_mean_bounded_by_construction), so it checks the implementation, not exchangeability with new scenes; the spread across scenes is the information",
  "mean_heldout_fnr_lo/hi": "0.95 percentile bootstrap over scenes (2000 replicates); descriptive only, since the folds share calibration scenes"
 },
 "caveats": [
  "The guarantee is marginal: an expectation over calibration sets and new scenes, every scene weighted equally; single scenes and strata (far, occluded, some classes) can exceed alpha.",
  "It assumes scenes exchangeable with the calibration scenes (same capture protocol and site population).",
  "Feasibility needs at least 1/alpha - 1 calibration scenes, and more the more the labeller misses.",
  "Object-views: an object seen in several views of a video counts once per view."
 ],
